  "Question": "How many degrees are in the smaller angle between the hour hand and the minute hand of a clock that reads seven o’clock?",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(50^\\circ\\)",
    "B": "\\(120^\\circ\\)",
    "C": "\\(135^\\circ\\)",
    "D": "\\(150^\\circ\\)",
    "E": "\\(165^\\circ\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "D",
  "Solution": "At seven o’clock, the minute hand points to \\(12\\) and the hour hand points to \\(7\\). The twelve equally spaced hour marks divide a full turn into angles of\n\\[\n360^\\circ\\div12=30^\\circ.\n\\]\nFrom \\(7\\) through \\(8,9,10,11\\) to \\(12\\) there are five intervals; the other direction has seven. Thus the smaller angle is \\(5\\times30^\\circ=150^\\circ\\), choice D.",
